  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a6ab2c78ad73481db040d9d4debb62be",
      "statement": "ProviderResolver's constructor is the sole admission gate for the provider list: it throws InvalidOperationException for an empty Agent:Providers list, for a Name repeated case-insensitively, for an Agent:General:Provider value that matches no entry Name, and for an Endpoint that is not an absolute URI — in that fixed order, so only the first problem is reported.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L21-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb1476050eb1307edd00cd5c314f809db6a6f3937fc490c01caed6601f93a81e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ProviderResolverTests.cs#L20-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:526760ffd52bace0dba23e7f8f0ea99d861315b76499d1a0b93da5530a8e98df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_965650f36a1e428684bca77c69807084",
      "statement": "Because Program.cs resolves ProviderResolver eagerly immediately after builder.Build(), every provider-configuration failure in the constructor aborts process startup instead of surfacing on the first webhook, while the resolver never contacts the endpoint so credential, model-id, and reachability problems can only fail later inside the first agent run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L40-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b36b1b1c86bb9d607d883845b284904cc9c67fc6b38a5dc26ebd25b756eb0b42:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L21-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb16f54d06e7ea862da6375f0b4ed0d9086240de715a1ef1e14ec5119c1902a7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L63-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:731d48a1012622f68a5d9d31c947e8e9b8d9f8a9ccc334b9fff2e2e7500d7c3e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1dd42639a19a4a7eba7c272c2acc99c9",
      "statement": "Provider selection matches Agent:General:Provider against provider Name with StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase and takes the first match; the preceding case-insensitive duplicate-name check is what makes that first-match lookup unambiguous, and each check uses StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L30-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36f33bd6338a4cb050b1ff2fa6c48ab7dabc071069e9ea7fa1a68b1effa7956c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ProviderResolverTests.cs#L30-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6957683ae575f736320bdebbc516c2dde5d4f75bbc7f11495dc464586ef523f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_04161858383147468e74fd7d7966ceb8",
      "statement": "The optional Endpoint falls back to the constant https://api.openai.com/v1 only when it is null, since the expression is selected.Endpoint ?? DefaultEndpoint; an explicitly empty string therefore reaches Uri.TryCreate and fails as 'has an invalid endpoint' rather than using the default, and the URI check is shape-only with no scheme or HTTP restriction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L15-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d93b1372e54dae5ac0eee952771ffdd89abcf9ff5b2ce8a9664a885bee8551b9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L42-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:552fc1da95669583df86465de89cc269890d01013b09836e3412052e6d6a9b6c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1960e924814f4ebd8f5710e95b0f21dc",
      "statement": "Agent:General:Model is a single process-wide scalar passed verbatim to OpenAIClient.GetChatClient(_model), so there is no per-role, per-provider, or per-job model selection; expressing a different model for another role would require changing CreateChatClient's signature or adding a second resolver.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L47-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10bc1e8435062e70694c07653902d9d79c4d08217a1becba00c5b77880752675:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Configuration/SebastianConfig.cs#L49-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39edca3e9b3330064a5affa4fd9e965e0e2f0ba3c92e784053b83a9cf473f55c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c0d89f80ec0b492a85ed22a1f982baa5",
      "statement": "CreateChatClient is a stateless factory over the three fields captured at construction: each call allocates a new OpenAIClient with an ApiKeyCredential and OpenAIClientOptions carrying only Endpoint, then adapts GetChatClient(_model) via AsIChatClient; the resolver is a process-wide singleton but the IChatClient is per job, and no retry, timeout, handler, or logging options are configured.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L40-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17345d4bffd2c1de6aa566b27a91133348207f6bae5b5587afceea8a707d5a09:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L52-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc595070289738ebf3b629ae81ed584d0c2577d60d0d76f0f5817e517e5676e1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3466a89e815f4266b62da345c0414c37",
      "statement": "The disposal contract is defensive rather than guaranteed: IChatClient is not promised to be IDisposable, so ImplementSpec disposes the returned client inside a finally guarded by `is IDisposable`, nested within the await-using on the role so the client is released before the role and its shell are torn down, including on exception; nothing in the suite asserts that disposal reaches the underlying OpenAI HTTP pipeline.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L38-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:57134e7d1172424ebf9d2cb7e47a8ddc37fb7614dd0ab339b4469bb3150239c5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ProviderResolverTests.cs#L9-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:669a2d306424fd0f0682e67f896ed19c9c07d382268f3b32211ce31f73567864:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9ae95735bc874dfa8a0d5d895d3d45f1",
      "statement": "Blank or whitespace-only provider values never reach ProviderResolver: [Required] on strings plus [ValidateObjectMembers] on Agent and [ValidateEnumeratedItems] on Agent.Providers means the source-generated ValidateSebastianConfig rejects them when IOptions.Value is materialized, which the constructor triggers on its first statement — pinned by BlankApiKeyIsRejectedByGeneratedValidator, which flips a valid config to failing by setting ApiKey to a single space.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Configuration/SebastianConfig.cs#L35-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e245fadd43843a0b009a080e3e9af6dcd71076a9803b7e8cce4764153d84895:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ProviderResolverTests.cs#L57-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0d95df3cd933a9f96bb529be2f42da3b7f45491596c0dde39ca3c0426e7ac4e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da6b07eb9b9944fc8403bdabbbfb6581",
      "statement": "Every element of Agent:Providers is validated, not only the selected one, because Agent.Providers carries [ValidateEnumeratedItems]; an unselected entry therefore still needs a non-blank Name and ApiKey to boot, but its Endpoint is never URI-checked since that check lives in ProviderResolver and applies only to the selected entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L38-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6dd4418b89bbefeb19a611da3d3d84b083073891a7f6286ddf5039db47b233f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Configuration/SebastianConfig.cs#L44-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0808b8fdce2ef3304a9707253d845dcf7fbb5e5139496ddce044e89544be0190:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e704a2c73259443c9611c2f996fdbf9a",
      "statement": "The repository proves only an OpenAI-compatible abstraction — API key credential, overridable base URL, and a free-form model id used with the OpenAI client stack — and defines no per-vendor behavior: provider names are opaque selection labels, no code maps a name to a URL or header, and nothing at this layer implements cost, rate, or quota control.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ProviderResolver.cs#L52-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc595070289738ebf3b629ae81ed584d0c2577d60d0d76f0f5817e517e5676e1:"
        },
        {
