          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:936d307533bbe6ca1222f3a75f397e4a602aca1cb641d7ab11bac9485a06047b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_73aee9a3e0b14acc972ef047983f0fa9",
      "statement": "ProviderResolverTests builds the resolver directly with Options.Create and never reaches the network: it pins the three exact constructor messages (empty list, duplicate name, missing provider) and only asserts NotNull on the created client, leaving the default endpoint constant, the invalid-endpoint message, the case-insensitive selection path, the model id actually passed to GetChatClient, and any disposal propagation unverified.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ProviderResolverTests.cs#L9-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:14fd8454e6f04d1c8e4605a157697fea4adcc3f4e7b8dbfcbc5cde2bbe6b12b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_465c3bea8fe84951b609638971146aa1",
      "statement": "ProviderResolver is the only file in the agent layer that suppresses OPENAI001 alongside MEAI001, marking the OpenAI client surface as experimental and keeping that dependency isolated from the harness files that instead suppress MAAI001/MEAI001 — relevant because the build uses TreatWarningsAsErrors with AnalysisLevel=latest-all.",
